# See README.md's "Environment Variables" section for how to get these values.

# The full, connection-specific inbound URL NEXTOSA generates for this site's Custom App
# connection (Settings > Integrations > Custom Apps in the NEXTOSA CRM). Used by the Contact
# form's Server Action (src/app/contact/actions.ts) to send new leads into NEXTOSA.
NEXTOSA_INBOUND_URL=https://your-nextosa-domain.example.com/api/webhooks/connected-apps/your-connection-id

# The shared secret for the SAME Custom App connection above - shown once, alongside
# NEXTOSA_INBOUND_URL, when you click "Generate Inbound API Key" in NEXTOSA. Used in BOTH
# directions: this site sends it as the x-api-key header when posting leads to NEXTOSA (see
# NEXTOSA_INBOUND_URL above), and verifies it as the HMAC-SHA256 signing key on commands NEXTOSA
# sends back to this site (src/app/api/webhooks/crm/route.ts's own x-nextosa-signature check).
CRM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=your-connection-inbound-api-key

# Contact form -> NEXTOSA API. The inquiry is stored for the Superadmin panel ("Website Inquiries" tab)
# and the owner is emailed instantly. NEXTOSA_API_URL is the API base INCLUDING /api (for example
# https://your-api.example.com/api); WEBSITE_INQUIRY_SECRET must equal the same-named variable on
# the API server (generate any long random string).
NEXTOSA_API_URL=http://localhost:4000/api
WEBSITE_INQUIRY_SECRET=
